inputs for a nosuchcity 2026 forecast

  [MISSING] 2026 voting districts
            have: —
            from: MDB FeatureServer
            do:   python src/fetch_boundaries.py --muni NOSUCHCITY
  [MISSING] 2026 wards
            have: —
            from: MDB FeatureServer
            do:   python src/fetch_boundaries.py --muni NOSUCHCITY
  [MISSING] 2026 voters' roll (registration)
            have: —
            from: elections.org.za/pw/StatsData/Voter-Registration-Statistics
            do:   province -> municipality in a BROWSER (the selector will not drive over plain HTTP), page the ward table, commit it as archive/iec-registration-<date>/nosuchcity_ward_registration_<date>.csv — that page keeps no archive
  [MISSING] national baseline
            have: 0 file(s) carrying registration
            from: IEC downloadable party results, per VD
            do:   python src/fetch_iec.py
  [MISSING] local baseline
            have: 0 file(s) carrying registration
            from: IEC downloadable party results, per VD
            do:   python src/fetch_iec.py
  [MISSING] 2026 certified party roster
            have: —
            from: IEC certified candidate lists
            do:   type the certified list into judgements/<city>-<target>.toml. ⛔ complete=true LICENSES DELETING every party it omits, so it needs the IEC's own list, not a newspaper's count of it

6 required input(s) not in hand: 2026 voting districts, 2026 wards, 2026 voters' roll (registration), national baseline, local baseline, 2026 certified party roster
A forecast run will NOT fail because of these. That is the point of this check: each of them has a silent fallback.
